  "create_dynamic_rite": {
    "name": {
      "rva": "0x481fb98",
      "file_offset": "0x481e998",
      "value": "create_dynamic_rite"
    },
    "native_help_text": {
      "rva": "0x481fbb0",
      "file_offset": "0x481e9b0",
      "value": "Creates a dynamic Rite within the Faith of the Character in scope.\nThe character will be the founder. Tenets and doctrines are inherited from the founder's current rite.\nFaith and founder are used to dynamically generate icon and names for the new Rite, based on the final tenet/doctrine state after overrides are applied.\n\nOptional overrides (applied before name/icon generation):\n  core_tenet_override_entry: replaces the tenets the founder likes least (by Spiritual Fulfillment). Max FAITH_CORE_TENETS_CAP entries; excess entries are ignored with an error.\n  doctrine_override_entry: if the rite already has a doctrine in the same group, that doctrine is replaced; otherwise the doctrine is added.\n\nIf a target divergence is specified and the overrides do not suffice to reach it, random tenets and doctrines will be added to the overrides until the threshold is reached.\n\n<scope:character> = {\n\tcreate_dynamic_rite = {\n\t\tsave_scope_as = new_rite\n\t\tconvert = no\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t# whether the founder should convert (default is no)\n\t\tcore_tenet_override_entry = tenet:some_tenet\t# tenet scope, may be repeated up to FAITH_CORE_TENETS_CAP times\n\t\tcore_tenet_override_entry = scope:saved_tenet\n\t\tdoctrine_override_entry = doctrine:some_doctrine\t# doctrine scope, may be repeated\n\n\t\ttarget_divergence = 0\t\t\t\t\t\t\t# reference amount of divergence the new rite has to have with respect to the mainline rite.\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t#\t0 is default and will be ignored. The final divergence could be a bit less or a bit more.\n\t\tinclude_unknown = no\t\t\t\t\t\t\t# allows to pick any tenet and doctrine, not just the ones known to the founder (default is no)\n\t\toverride_tenets_first = yes\t\t\t\t\t\t# if yes the effect will try to change tenets before changing doctrines. \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t#\tif no it will change doctrines first. default is yes.\n\t}\n}"
    },
